> Downstairs, seven people are arguing gently about how to spend the last seventy minutes. Justin isn't one of them.
> You don't have to ask where he went. The second-floor corridor is dark except for one door at the very end, propped open with a sneaker.
> Your feet know this corridor. One winter, you walked it every night with the keys, checking the rooms were empty.
