> The mirrors are dusty. Someone has drawn a smiley face in the dust on one of them.
> Low down. At the height of a person sitting on the floor.
> And Justin is dancing.
> Not the way he danced on the wet pavement, or across the lobby, or for anyone.
> Slowly. A long reach. A turn that takes four whole counts. A weight shift so gradual it almost isn't one.
> He's not very good at it.
> That's the first thing you notice, and it surprises you.
> He rushes the turn. He hurries through the reach like he's embarrassed to be caught in the middle of it.
> His lips are moving. Counting. In Japanese.
@show justin surprised at=c
> He sees you in the mirror, and the whole thing vanishes. Instantly. Like a tab closed.
