> He spins, and points at his own reflection. The reflection, obviously, points back.
justin: —featuring my reflection, who has been late to every single rehearsal. Look at him. Half a beat behind. Unprofessional.
> He argues with the mirror. He does both sides. It's genuinely funny. He's very good at this.
> He's also breathing a little too fast, and he hasn't looked at you straight on since you walked in.
* [playful] Laugh. It really is funny.
    @rel justin closeness+1
    justin[laugh]: Thank you! Thank you. He'll be here all night. Well. Until five.
* [quiet] Don't laugh. Just watch him.
    @rel justin trust+1
    > The bit runs out of road. He keeps it going a few seconds longer anyway, on his own, like a wheel still spinning after the bike has stopped.
