* [quiet] Put your hand in his without a word.
    @rel justin trust+1
    > He looks at your hand in his for a second, like he's memorising the count.
> His other hand settles lightly at your back. Asking more than holding. You nod. It stays.
> He counts, at first. Under his breath, in Japanese, so quietly it's almost just breathing. *Ichi, ni, san, shi.*
> Around the second eight, you step on his foot. He doesn't make it a bit. He just laughs, low, and adjusts.
> Around the third eight, he stops counting.
> It isn't the good dance or the bad one. It's slow, and it wobbles, and he doesn't cover the wobble with anything.
> There's nowhere to hide in the slow parts. He doesn't try.
@music justin
